% What lesson 4's two readings of a missing record should say.
% A fact must be derived; `:- fact.` must never be, and may use variables.
%
%   python3 diagnose.py programs/missing-data.dl --expect programs/missing-data.expect
%   python3 mutation.py programs/missing-data.dl --expect programs/missing-data.expect

eligible(bob).                   % checked, and not employed
eligible_naive(bob).
eligible_naive(dana).            % the naive rule's mistake, which is the lesson
:- eligible(dana).               % never checked: no evidence either way
pending(dana).                   % ...so she is sent to be checked
:- pending(bob).
:- eligible(cyril).              % checked, and employed
:- eligible_naive(cyril).
